    "National Council on Disability. Quality-Adjusted Life Years and the Devaluation of Life with a Disability. Washington DC, 2019. Found sufficient evidence of discriminatory effects of QALYs to recommend prohibition, and recommended that Congress prohibit Medicare and Medicaid from using the QALY.": {"url":"https://www.ncd.gov/report/quality-adjusted-life-years-and-the-devaluation-of-life-with-a-disability/","verified_by":"official-ncd-page","checked_at":"2026-08-30"},
    "National Council on Independent Living. Resolution Opposing the Use of QALYs (Quality Adjusted Life Years), adopted 23 July 2020. NCIL is a cross-disability grassroots organization run by and for people with disabilities; the resolution states that NCIL opposes the use of the QALY in all decisions concerning health care coverage and commits to supporting state and federal efforts to prohibit it.": {"url":"https://ncil.org/about/ncil-documents-forms/resolutions/resolution-opposing-the-use-of-qalys-quality-adjusted-life-years/","verified_by":"official-ncil-page","checked_at":"2026-08-30"},
    "National Institute for Health and Care Excellence. NICE health technology evaluations: the manual (PMG36). The reference case regards all QALYs as being of equal weight; severity is assessed by absolute and proportional shortfall and applied as a quantitative QALY weight of x1.2 or x1.7, with further modifiers considered qualitatively in committee deliberation.": {"url":"https://www.nice.org.uk/process/pmg36","verified_by":"official-nice-page","checked_at":"2026-08-30"},
